	issn = {1064-1734, 2164-7313},
	doi = {10.1080/10641734.2025.2498996},
	abstract = {This paper explores the application of large language models (LLMs) such as ChatGPT in advertising and communication research, emphasizing their foundational processes, research applications, and ethical implications. We provide an overview of LLMs meant to be accessible to non-computer science specialists. We review the existing literature to highlight common uses of LLMs in academic research, which yields three categories: LLM output testing, LLM tools, and LLM-to-human comparison. We also discuss limitations, ethical considerations and practical challenges in employing LLMs for advertising and media studies and provide insights for effective application. This overview underscores the significance of bridging theoretical understanding and practical use of LLMs while maintaining ethical integrity.},
